# Copy to .env.local for local development, and set the same values in
# Vercel > Project > Settings > Environment Variables for deployments.
#
# Nothing here is required to run the site: without it the chat widget shows
# the "call us / book a call" fallback and enquiries are only written to the
# server log. Logs are not durable storage, so set the Aleesa variables
# before launch.

# ---- Chat assistant: Aleesa Web Chat (preferred) --------------------
# Set BOTH and the Aleesa provider takes over from ANTHROPIC_API_KEY below.
# The bot is then trained in the Aleesa dashboard - Knowledge Base plus the
# Chat Agent - so `assistantSystemPrompt` in src/lib/site.ts is NOT used,
# and every conversation lands in the Aleesa inbox where a human can take
# over.
#
# Setup, once:
#   1. Aleesa dashboard > Settings > Connections > Web Chat > "Enable Web
#      Chat". That generates the tenant API key; copy it there and then -
#      afterwards only a masked version is shown, and regenerating it
#      invalidates the old key immediately.
#   2. Paste it as ALEESA_WEBCHAT_API_KEY below.
#   3. ALEESA_WEBHOOK_URL is the Aleesa *webhook server* origin, with no
#      trailing path - "/webhooks/web-chat" is appended by the adapter.
#      Pasting the full endpoint works too; the path is not doubled.
#   4. Verify with "Test Web Chat" in the same dashboard card before
#      pointing the site at it.
#
# The key is a server-only secret: it identifies the tenant and anyone
# holding it can post as this site. Never rename it with a NEXT_PUBLIC_
# prefix - it is read in src/lib/chat/aleesa-provider.ts, which only ever
# runs in the /api/chat route handler.
ALEESA_WEBHOOK_URL=
ALEESA_WEBCHAT_API_KEY=

# ---- Enquiries -> Aleesa CRM (Website Form intake) ------------------
# Set BOTH and every enquiry - contact, house & land, property management,
# property sales, Boutique Chevron Island - is filed in Aleesa as a Lead
# with source "website_form", carrying the full submission.
#
# Setup, once:
#   1. Aleesa dashboard > Settings > Connections > Website Form >
#      "Enable Website Form". Copy the key there and then - afterwards only
#      a masked version is shown, and regenerating it invalidates the old
#      key immediately.
#   2. Paste it as ALEESA_WEBSITE_FORM_API_KEY below.
#   3. ALEESA_API_URL is the Aleesa *API* origin - a DIFFERENT host from
#      ALEESA_WEBHOOK_URL above. Either an origin or the full submit URL
#      works: "/api/v1/integrations/website-form/submit" is appended by the
#      adapter only when it is not already there.
#
#      Heads up: the dashboard card can print the submit URL against
#      "api-aleesa.ai", which does not resolve. It derives that host from
#      the browser URL when the dashboard's own API base is unset. The host
#      that answers is api.aleesa.ai - hyphen to dot.
#
# Server-only secret, like the web chat key: anyone holding it can file
# leads as this tenant.
ALEESA_API_URL=https://api.aleesa.ai
ALEESA_WEBSITE_FORM_API_KEY=

# ---- Chat assistant: Claude (fallback) ------------------------------
# Used only when the two ALEESA_WEBCHAT variables above are unset. The bot
# is then trained by `assistantSystemPrompt` in src/lib/site.ts, holds no
# memory between page loads, and conversations are not recorded anywhere.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
